Experiment - (b): Display lines b/w start and end line numbers using shell script passed as arguments.

Steps:
1. Open Terminal.
2. Create the script -> nano 6b.sh
3. Enter -> #!/bin/bash
read -p "Enter file name : " file
read -p "Enter starting line number : " start
read -p "Enter ending line number : " end
sed -n "${start},${end}p" "$file"
4. Save using Ctrl + O -> Enter and exit using Ctrl + X.
5. Give execution permission -> chmod +x exp6b.sh
6. (i) Create a sample file -> nano test.txt
(ii) Enter several lines, save and exit.
7. Run the filename, starting line and ending line when asked.

Result: The specified range of lines is displayed from the file.
